COMMUNITY

More Than Racing

The Obstacle Course Racing Association of Ireland (OCRA ÉIREANN) exists to support more than competition alone.

Obstacle racing has always been built around community.

People may come to OCR because they want to race, improve their fitness or learn new skills, but many stay because of the friendships, clubs, training groups and shared experiences that develop around the sport.


The Irish OCR Community

The obstacle racing community in Ireland includes:

- Recreational athletes
- Competitive athletes
- Elite athletes
- Age Group athletes
- Youth athletes
- Adaptive athletes
- Clubs
- Training groups
- Coaches
- Technical Officials
- Race organisers
- Volunteers
- Gyms and training facilities
- Families and supporters

Each plays a role in helping the sport grow.


Getting Involved

There are many ways to become part of the OCR community.

You can:

